{"type":"text","timestamp":1792244755892,"sessionID":"ses_eb5e52a9effeKHO4XQV4Er1qkQ","part":{"id":"prt_14a1c70a9001PHRTVgMGPSjx6W_text-0","sessionID":"ses_eb5e52a9effeKHO4XQV4Er1qkQ","messageID":"msg_14a1c70a9001PHRTVgMGPSjx6W","type":"text","text":"I've reached the maximum number of steps for this task, so I'm stopping here with a summary. Please note that I was unable to run `node --test` — shell execution was denied by the environment — so I implemented the code by carefully tracing through each test case manually instead.\n\n## What was accomplished\n\n**`src/csv.mjs` — `parseCSV` (implemented, polished):**\n- Character-level state machine parser supporting:\n- Quoted fields, including commas inside quotes (`\"Smith, Jo\"`)\n- Escaped quotes (`\"he said \"\"hi\"\"\"` → `he said \"hi\"`)\n- Newlines inside quoted fields (kept in the field)\n- CRLF line endings\n- Missing trailing newline (final row is still emitted)\n- Empty fields preserved (`a,,c` and `,,` both keep empty entries)\n- Completely empty lines produce no row (`''` and `'\\n'` → `[]`), which the tests require, while comma-only lines (`,,`) still produce a row\n- Unclosed quote (e.g. `a\\n\"oops\\n`) throws an error matching `/unterminated/i`\n\n**`src/report.mjs` — `summarize` (implemented):**\n- Parses the CSV, finds header indices for `groupBy` and `sum`, and throws `unknown column: <name>` when either is missing\n- Skips blank lines the parser does not emit (they're already excluded)\n- Throws an error matching `/not a number/i` for empty or non-numeric sum values\n- Groups by the `groupBy` value, sums the `sum` column, counts rows per group\n- Rounds totals to two decimals via `Math.round(total * 100) / 100` (handles the `0.1 + 0.2` case)\n- Returns `{ group, total, count }` objects sorted by group name\n\n## What remains\n\n- **Verification**: I was not able to execute `node --test` in this environment (shell permission was denied). All test cases were traced by hand and should pass, but that has not been confirmed by actually running the test suite.\n- Nothing outside `src/` was modified; the `test/` directory is untouched, as required.\n\n## Recommended next step\n\nRun `node --test` in the project root to confirm all tests pass. If anything fails, it will likely be a subtle edge case in the parser (e.g., whitespace handling or empty-line semantics) that can be fixed with a small adjustment to the relevant branch in `src/csv.mjs`.","time":{"start":1792244740295,"end":1792244755892}}}
